## 3. Detailed Proposed Changes

### Component 1: Intent Router & Classification Repair
#### [MODIFY] [server.py](file:///d:/DATATHON/DATATHON/backend/routes.py) / [server.py (standalone)](file:///d:/DATATHON/DATATHON/backend/app.py)
- Replace hardcoded fallback to `ANALYTICAL`.
- If LLM router fails or query asks qualitative questions (`why`, `what can we do`, `how to prevent`, `SOP`, `recommendations`), default to **`STRATEGIC_ADVISORY`**.
- Explicit Trigger Rules:
  - If prompt contains explicit chart verbs (`show chart`, `plot`, `statistics`, `bar chart`, `graph`): Route to `DATA_QUERY` (`render_visuals: true`).
  - If prompt contains strategic verbs (`why`, `what can we do`, `explain`, `SOP`): Route to `STRATEGIC_ADVISORY` (`render_visuals: false`).

### Component 2: Advisory Strategy Agent (`AdvisoryStrategyAgent`)
#### [NEW] [advisory_agent.py](file:///d:/DATATHON/DATATHON/backend/advisory_agent.py)
- Implements `BaseAgent`.
- Silently queries top district numbers (e.g. Whitefield) without building chart payloads.
- Uses `STRATEGIC_ADVISORY_PROMPT` to produce executive situational thesis, causal operational dynamics, and P1/P2/P3 actionable directives.
- Returns `render_visuals: false`.

### Component 3: Frontend Canvas Preservation Logic
#### [MODIFY] [Chatbot.jsx](file:///d:/DATATHON/DATATHON/frontend/src/components/Chatbot.jsx)
- Update `handleSendMessage`:
  - When backend response arrives with `render_visuals: false`, update chat messages feed, but **DO NOT reset or clear active chart state** in `selectedModalChart` / left panel canvas.
  - Keeps the previous graph visible on the left while displaying the officer's strategic answer in the right feed!

